    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d202">

                <pb facs="0291" n="277" sameAs="frus:frus1945v09/pg277"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.62115/8–3045: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Costa Rica</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gibson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">San Jose</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-08-30T17:00:00-06:00">August 30, 1945—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 10:13 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>514. Supreme Court of Costa Rica by vote of 14 to 3 today issued writ of habeas
                    corpus directed [<hi rendition="#italic">directing?</hi>] President of Republic
                    to produce body of Franz Amrhein a German civilian internee in the United States
                    from Costa Rica. Similar writs will probably follow in quick order in favor of
                    other German internees. Despatch follows.<anchor n="21" xml:id="d202-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gibson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
